 of the first paper reporting the genetic study on the COGA</comment></citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zinn-Justin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Abel</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genome search for alcohol dependence using the weighted pairwise correlation linkage method: interesting findings on chromosome 4</article-title><source>Genet. Epidemiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>S421</fpage><lpage>S426</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10597473</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dunn</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Hinrichs</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bertelsen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Jin</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kauwe</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Suarez</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Bierut</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Microsatellites versus single-nucleotide polymorphisms in linkage analysis for quantitative and qualitative measures</article-title><source>BMC Genet</source><year>2005</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>S122</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16451580</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dick</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Aliev</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Saccone</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hinrichs</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Berte